mod:silent_trip_road_meets_the_back_road;
// THE PRICE OF THE SILENT TRIP (DEF-570, landing 177d2b2): TWO RIGHT PROGRAMS, REFUSED. A jump out of an inner loop to something
// around the enclosing loop is first met on the enclosing loop's silent trip, where its road is held and then met with the inner
// loop's back road whole. So a permit the road set itself is lowered where the back road lacks it: `wl1_price` (a `Result`
// tested on the road that continues the outer loop and read at its head: TAINT-001) and `wl4_price` (a local assigned on the
// road that gives from the inner loop: ASSIGN-001). Both compiled and ran right before this landing. The remedies are in the
// program beside this file: test again at the read (`wl1r`), assign at the declaration (`wl4r`).
//   The controls, wrong programs of the same shapes, refused at the same place: the road doesn't test (`wl1c`: `.value` of an
//   error, 60, accepted before this landing) or doesn't assign (`wl4c`, `wl3c`).
//   A channel whose roads a `defer` body all ended stays dead through the meet, which skips a channel dead after the merge (`wr1`, `wr2`, beside this file); the same
//   jumps alive are refused (`wr1k`, `wr2k`).
// THE SAME MEET'S OTHER PRICE (P-1, landing 177d2b2): A DEAD JUMP'S STAMP WIDENS AN EARLIER LIVE ROAD. A jump stamps its channel whenever its own state is live, whatever its `defer` bodies do to the road,
// and the meet acts on the whole channel, so a live road sent before the inner loop is lowered too: `pw1_price`, `pw2_price`, right programs, 67 before this landing, TAINT-001 here. It needs a live `break` or
// `continue` sent earlier, an inner silent loop and a `defer` body that never ends, on the same road. It isn't DEF-570's, whose road loses what it set itself: this road was sent before the trip. The controls and
// the remedy are beside this file: no dead jump (`pw1k`), no earlier road (`pw1e`), test again at the read (`pw1r`, `pw2r`).
mod:wl1_price_continue_outer_keeps_permit = {
error:E5_wl1_price_continue_outer_keeps_permit;
struct:H = { string:s; int64:k; };
func:mkh = H() never fails { pass H{ s: string_concat("ab", "cde"), k: 7i64 }; };
func:eath = int64(move H:v) never fails { pass 0i64; };
func:ok = int64() { pass 7i64; };
func:bad = int64() { fail E5_wl1_price_continue_outer_keeps_permit; };
func:okn = int64(int64:n) { if (n > 90i64) { fail E5_wl1_price_continue_outer_keeps_permit; } pass 7i64; };
func:f = int64(int64:n) never fails {
    int64:out = 0i64;
    Result<int64>:r = ok(); if (r.is_error) { pass 1i64; }
    int64:i = 0i64;
    outer: while (i < 3i64) decreases 3i64 - i {
        i = i + 1i64;
        out = r.value;
        r = okn(n);
        int64:k = 0i64;
        while (k < 2i64) decreases 2i64 - k {
            k = k + 1i64;
            if (n > 1i64) { r = ok(); if (r.is_error) { pass 1i64; } continue outer; }
        }
        r = ok(); if (r.is_error) { pass 1i64; }
    }
    pass out;
};
};
